# Walkthrough - Facility Management Page

I have successfully implemented the Facility Management page, allowing users to view, create, edit, and delete facilities.

## Changes

### Frontend

#### [NEW] [types/index.ts](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/types/index.ts)
- Defined [Facility](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/types/index.ts#3-14) interface and [FacilityType](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/types/index.ts#1-2) enum to ensure type safety across the application.

#### [NEW] [components/facilities/FacilityList.tsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/facilities/FacilityList.tsx)
- Displays facilities in a responsive grid layout.
- Handles empty states and loading states.
- Provides "Edit" and "Delete" actions for each facility.

#### [NEW] [components/facilities/FacilityForm.tsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/facilities/FacilityForm.tsx)
- Form for creating and editing facilities.
- Includes validation for required fields.
- Handles API requests (POST/PUT) and error management.

#### [MODIFY] [app/dashboard/facilities/page.tsx](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/app/dashboard/facilities/page.tsx)
- Integrated [FacilityList](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/facilities/FacilityList.tsx#13-112) and [FacilityForm](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/cement/frontend/src/components/facilities/FacilityForm.tsx#22-162).
- Implemented state management to toggle between list view and form view.
- Added a "Create Facility" button to trigger the form.

